  "prefLabel": "Par 211.01 Waiver of Suspension of Rules",
  "priorExpiration": "2008-07-09",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Par 211.01 Waiver of Suspension of Rules. The presiding officer, upon the motion of any party or intervener, or on his own initiative, shall suspend or waive any requirement or limitation imposed by this chapter when the suspension or waiver:\n\n(a) Appears to be lawful; and\n\n(b) Is more likely to promote the just, accurate, and efficient resolution of the pending dispute than would adherence to a particular rule or procedures.\n\nSource. #7149, eff 12-7-99, EXPIRED: 12-7-07\n\nNew. #9070, INTERIM, eff 1-11-08, EXPIRED: 7-9-08\n\nNew. #9254, eff 9-6-08; ss by #12157, eff 4-7-17 (from Par 212.01)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/par100-500.html"
